    </div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0112]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0118" num="0112" class="description-line">As seen above, in Table 1 and Table 2, the microporous polyethylene film prepared in accordance with the present invention exhibited very superior puncture strength and thermal stability at high temperature and showed less decrease of permeability due to low thermal shrinkage at high temperature, as well as superior permeability. Therefore, it can be usefully applied in a high-capacity, high-output battery.</div>
    </li> <li> <para-num num="[0113]"> </para-num> <div id="p-0119" num="0113" class="description-line">Although the preferred embodiments of the invention have been disclosed for illustrative purposes, those skilled in the art will appreciate that various modifications, additions and substitutions are possible, without departing from the scope and spirit of the invention as disclosed in the accompanying claims.</div>
    
  </li> </ul>
  </div>
  </section>

  <section itemprop="claims" itemscope>
    <h2>Claims (<span itemprop="count">3</span>)</h2>
    
    <div itemprop="content" html><div mxw-id="PCLM8227747" lang="EN" load-source="patent-office" class="claims">
  <div class="claim"> <div id="CLM-00001" num="00001" class="claim">
    <div class="claim-text"> <b>1</b>. A microporous polyethylene film prepared from a raw mixture comprising 20-50 wt % polyethylene and 80-50 wt % diluent, which has a film thickness of 5-40 μm, a porosity of 35-55%, a permeability from 2.5 10<sup>−5 </sup>to 10.0 10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy, a puncture strength of at least 0.10 N/μm at 90° C., a puncture angle of at least 30° at 90° C., and a permeability from 2.0 10<sup>−5 </sup>to 8.0 10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy after shrinking freely at 120° C. for 1 hour.</div>
  </div>
  </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00002" num="00002" class="claim">
    <div class="claim-text"> <b>2</b>. The microporous polyethylene film as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein polyethylene has a weight average molecular weight from 2.0 10<sup>5 </sup>to 4.5 10<sup>5</sup>.</div>
  </div>
  </div> <div class="claim-dependent"> <div id="CLM-00003" num="00003" class="claim">
    <div class="claim-text"> <b>3</b>. The microporous polyethylene film as set forth in <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, which has a film thickness of 9-25 μm, a porosity of 35-50%, a permeability from 3.0×10<sup>−5 </sup>to 8.0 10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy, a puncture strength of at least 0.12 N/μm at 90° C., a puncture angle of at least 32° at 90° C., and a permeability from 2.5 10<sup>−5 </sup>to 7.0 10<sup>−5 </sup>Darcy after shrinking freely at 120° C. for 1 hour. </div>
  </div>
</div> </div>
  </div>
  </section>

